{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2998","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2998","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2998\",\"parent_revision\":\"880b3c6f7e9d3073eda155054e19c0332e41aacb3d5f1bb8713d0b34887f4616\",\"root_revision\":\"880b3c6f7e9d3073eda155054e19c0332e41aacb3d5f1bb8713d0b34887f4616\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nList `.claude/agent-memory/` and verify: of the roughly 29 `dh:` agents in `plugins/development-harness/agents/`, only `impact-analyst` and `service-docs-maintainer` currently have any memory directory under `.claude/agent-memory/`. The judgment-heavy grooming-pipeline agents \u2014 `classifier`, `rtica-assessor`, `fact-checker`, `alignment-analyst`, `backlog-item-groomer` \u2014 have none. These are exactly the agents most likely to face the same repeated judgment call across many backlog items (e.g. \\\"is this really a `missing-guardrail` or a `defect`?\\\", \\\"is this fact actually verifiable from a primary source or should it be marked MISSING?\\\") with zero accumulated session-to-session experience to draw on, unlike e.g. `impact-analyst`, which does accumulate memory.\\n\\nSeparately \u2014 confirmed directly by listing `.claude/agent-memory/` in this session: there are two memory directories for what is the same agent \u2014 `dh-service-docs-maintainer` (5.1KB `dh-mcp-cli-docs.md` + 299-byte `MEMORY.md`, dated Aug 7) and `service-docs-maintainer` (1.9KB `MEMORY.md` only, dated Jun 2). This is the identical \\\"same identity, two independently-spelled representations, no canonical resolution\\\" failure shape as the backlog section-name bug this session spent ~2 hours fixing (#2956/#2970), just at the agent-memory-directory-name layer instead of the backlog-section-key layer: whatever mechanism derives a memory directory name from an agent's identity is producing two different answers for the same agent, causing memories written under one name to be invisible to a session that looks under the other.\\n\\nCandidate direction (not a required approach \u2014 investigate before committing): (1) establish a canonical rule for deriving an agent's memory-directory name from its plugin-qualified name (e.g. always `<plugin>-<agent-name>`, never a bare agent name, resolved by one shared function rather than left to convention at each memory-write call site) and fix the `service-docs-maintainer` split by merging the two directories under the canonical name; (2) extend the existing memory-writing pattern (used by `impact-analyst`/`service-docs-maintainer`) to `classifier`, `rtica-assessor`, `fact-checker`, and `alignment-analyst` \u2014 giving each agent instructions for what's worth remembering across sessions (e.g. classifier: past mis-classifications later corrected by a human; rtica-assessor: RT-ICA calls that later proved wrong; fact-checker: sources that turned out unreliable) and where its memory directory canonically lives.\\n\\nRelated but different scope: #2927 (worktree-isolated delegation prompts not specifying `.claude/agent-memory/` write handling for uncommitted files) \u2014 that issue is about commit/cleanup handling of memory writes already happening; this issue is about which agents have a memory directory at all, plus the confirmed split-brain duplicate-directory bug for `service-docs-maintainer`.\\n\\nThis is a P2 \u2014 a real, compounding quality gap (both the missing-memory issue and the confirmed split-brain directory bug), but not a live production incident.\\n\\n---\\nProcess note: `/dh:work-backlog-item create -- \\\"...\\\"` failed twice in this session with `Shell command failed for pattern \\\"!`...`\\\": (eval):1: permission denied: ../..` when invoked from a git worktree checkout (`.claude/worktrees/section-roundtrip-tests`) rather than the main repo checkout \u2014 reproducible regardless of the `create` argument content, isolated to the skill's `<gate_token>` line (`!`node \\\"${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs\\\"`\\\\`) failing to resolve `CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR` correctly from a nested worktree path. Running `node plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/scripts/get-gate-token.mjs` directly via Bash worked fine and produced a valid token, used here as a manual fallback. This item was filed via direct `backlog_add` MCP call with that manually-generated token rather than via the skill. This worktree/CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR resolution bug itself may warrant a separate backlog item if it recurs.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **agent-memory coverage gap for grooming-pipeline agents, plus confirmed split-brain duplicate memory directory for service-docs-maintainer** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 worktree section-roundtrip-tests, 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ce0123b0b10eb409ffc6bb4f0dc156128f9ba7bc4dcc5fc93bcca67af4743ba5\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgvfjQ\"}"}